      "message": "I don\u0027t agree with the introduction of this new log helper, though we can discuss about the need for a non fatal checker.\n\nOne of the main goals for adding the log library was to unify log behaviors, and make logs more deterministic. In particular I decided to remove everything that made use of NDEBUG to force similar behaviors between production and release builds.\n\nAdding assert_that_softly goes against this as the behavior is conditional on the platform.\n\nNow it might be useful to have a soft version of assert_that, e.g. check_that,\ndepending on how you plan on using it.",
